                <pb facs="0279" n="223" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg223"/>

                <head>No. 121.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoffman to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-05-02"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 2,
                        1876</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Winslow applies for <hi rendition="#italic">habeas corpus</hi> to-morrow. British
                    government will oppose his immediate release. Shall not intervene unless
                    instructed. Papers asked for in House of Commons; refused for the present.</p>
                <closer><signed>HOFFMAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
